% ============================================================================
% tooth-parts.query.adj — a worked recall over the anatomy tooth-parts library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is the enamel?": it
% states no anatomy fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `tooth_part_role` rows and returns the role + the table's source/locator/
% trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the role
% `covers_roots`, recall which part it is — cementum). A word that is not one of
% these tooth parts abstains honestly — the engine never invents a role.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli tooth-parts.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "tooth-parts.adj"

? tooth_part_role(enamel, $Role)      % expect outer_surface
? tooth_part_role(dentin, $Role)      % expect beneath_enamel
? tooth_part_role(pulp, $Role)        % expect blood_vessels_and_nerves
? tooth_part_role($Part, covers_roots) % reverse bind — expect cementum
? tooth_part_role(femur, $Role)       % expect abstain — the femur is a leg bone, not a tooth part
